quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  5,24,"They said: ‘O Musa (Moses)! We will never enter it as long as they remain there. So, go ahead, you and your Lord, and you both fight. We shall stay right here.’"
  5,25,He (Musa [Moses]) said: ‘My Lord! I have no control (over anyone) except for myself and my brother (Harun [Aaron]). So separate us from the rebellious people.’
  5,26,"(The Lord) said: ‘So this (land) shall be forbidden to them for forty years, while they will be wandering through the earth aimlessly. So do not grieve over the rebellious people.’"
  5,27,(Esteemed Prophet!) Relate to them with truth the story of Adam’s two sons (Habil and Qabil [Abel and Cain]): Each of them offered a sacrifice. It was accepted from one of them (Habil [Abel]) and was not from the other (Qabil [Cain]). He (Qabil) said: ‘I will most certainly slay you.’ He (Habil) replied: ‘Indeed Allah accepts (offering) only from the God-conscious.
  5,28,"Even if you extend your hand towards me to kill me, I will not extend my hand towards you to kill you. Indeed, I fear Allah, the Lord of all worlds."
  5,29,I desire you to bear (the burden of) my sin (i.e. the sin of killing me) and also your (other) sins (i.e. the preceding ones for which your offering was rejected). You will then become an inhabitant of the Fire. And that is the recompense of the wrongdoers.’
  5,30,"Then his soul prompted him to slay his brother, so he killed him; thus, he became one of the losers."
  5,31,"Then Allah sent a crow, scratching into the earth, to show him how he might bury the dead body of his brother. He said: ‘Oh, woe to me! Am I unable to be as this crow and bury my brother’s corpse?’ And he became one of the regretful."
